WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.910
- You've had another baby this year.

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:02.743
You were just talking about it.

00:00:02.743 --> 00:00:04.920
So that's, I am a mom as
well and work as well.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.130
And that's a hard thing to balance.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.550
Are you finding that hard?

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.100
- I mean, last night I
was up a good four times

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.127
in the night, you know, like, waiting,

00:00:12.127 --> 00:00:14.530
"Do I put the paci in, do I not?"

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.363
- Did you sleep train?

00:00:15.363 --> 00:00:16.196
Are you doing sleep training?

00:00:16.196 --> 00:00:17.029
- [Kirsten] We're in
the midst of it, yeah.

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:18.030
- Oh, you're in hell.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:18.863
- Yeah, I am.

00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:20.010
But my friend taught me a trick

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.300
to just put like 20 pacis around them.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.580
So they just go like this
and there, they find one.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.498
- 100 percent.

00:00:25.498 --> 00:00:27.170
- You know, just like as
many as can go in that crib.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.310
- Yeah, throw them all in.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.270
- Yeah, all of them.
- And especially the ones

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:30.577
with the little like penguins attached

00:00:30.577 --> 00:00:31.410
and all the little things.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.880
- Oh, I don't do those for some reason.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.190
- Oh, they, yeah, they gave them to me

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.897
and I just put anything in
there to get them to stop, yeah.

00:00:35.897 --> 00:00:36.956
- It's like, how do you wash them though?

00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:37.789
Wash the?

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:38.780
- [Kelly] The washing machine.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.613
You can put that part, yeah.

00:00:39.613 --> 00:00:40.700
- You just throw the whole thing in?

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.046
- Yeah, I think we did.
- With the paci attached.

00:00:42.046 --> 00:00:42.879
- I don't know if we were supposed to,

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:43.712
I'm pretty sure we did.

00:00:43.712 --> 00:00:44.545
- I don't know, I'm always
like, how do you wash it?

00:00:44.545 --> 00:00:45.378
It seems gross.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.211
Like it keeps dropping on the floor,

00:00:46.211 --> 00:00:47.362
it has a stuffed animal that's
just like sweeping the floor.

00:00:47.362 --> 00:00:49.270
- I know, I wasn't a
good like first-time mom.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.950
I was like, "That's free probiotics."

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.050
I'm like, if it was on the
floor, I'm like, "You're fine."

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.900
So is it true though
that your three-year-old

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.260
calls you treat mom?

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.380
- Treat mom, yes,

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.740
because I guess I give
him a lot of treats.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.450
And he also calls me trash mom too,

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:05.460
because I take all his trash.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.661
- That's different sounding.

00:01:06.661 --> 00:01:07.650
- I know.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.350
I'm treat mom and trash mom.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.120
- [Kelly] Trash mom is
a whole different story.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.080
- I know, It's literally
like, "Here, I'm done."

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:13.913
That's why he calls me trash mom.

00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:15.562
- I love it, oh, I love it.

00:01:15.562 --> 00:01:16.522
- Because when he's done, yeah.

00:01:16.522 --> 00:01:17.355
- Oh, yeah, I've started
implementing, my kids,

00:01:17.355 --> 00:01:18.777
I'm like, "Oh, look at
those legs you have.

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:20.340
"You can walk it on over yourself."

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.630
Yeah, they're five and seven.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.463
Mine are a little older, but yeah.

00:01:22.463 --> 00:01:26.110
But have you had any chance to
like take time for yourself?

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.840
I know it's hard, like
as moms, we always feel,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.770
I feel like all my
girlfriends that are moms,

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.240
you get that guilt of like
having time for yourself,

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.320
but it's like so important.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.153
Do you do that?

00:01:34.153 --> 00:01:36.440
- I also have the guilt of like,

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.310
I can't sit and watch a television show.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.450
Like if they're in the other room,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.360
you know, I just feel
like I don't have, yeah,

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.650
I haven't done really much
for myself, it's true.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:44.540
- Yeah, oh, do it.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.210
- Yeah, like once in a while

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.670
I'll go do something for my mental health

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.270
like go do a Pilates class,

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.710
even just to get my strength back

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.640
because I just felt like I
was hunched over in a chair

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.794
for three months, you know what I mean?

00:01:54.794 --> 00:01:55.627
It was like-
- 100 percent.

00:01:55.627 --> 00:01:56.594
- [Kirsten] Yeah.

00:01:56.594 --> 00:01:57.550
- Girl, I think that's
all I do in all my jobs.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.030
I sit in a chair.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.350
- I know, getting hair and makeup done.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.390
- [Kelly] That's all I do.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.383
- Yeah, me too, just
sitting in different chairs.

00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:03.993
- My hips are almost 40.

